# scripts/watch-check.sh's source list. Copy to ~/.config/lss/watch-sources.txt and edit -
# these two rows are EXAMPLES, not defaults; card #116 shipped an hourly systemd timer that
# runs against whatever is here (or nothing - an empty/comment-only file is fine, see below).
#
#   cp packaging/watch-sources.txt.example ~/.config/lss/watch-sources.txt
#
# One source per line, "|"-separated: <name>|<what this source's recipes actually feed, plain
# English>|<owner>/<repo> on GitHub. Blank lines and lines starting with # are skipped - so a
# file with nothing uncommented (the state right after this copy, until you edit it) is a valid
# empty list: the WATCH page then shows nothing, not an error.
#
# sglang|serving engine releases (what we run the serve on)|sgl-project/sglang
# vllm|the other major serving engine, for cross-checking release notes|vllm-project/vllm
